{"name":"Genevieve","hex":"#bcc4e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Genevieve","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from French."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Genevieve"}],"entries":[{"title":"Genevieve","blocks":[{"text":"Genevieve was a consecrated virgin, and is one of the patron saints of Paris in the Catholic Church, and she is also venerated in the Eastern Orthodox Church. Her feast day is on 3 January."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/StGenevieve.jpg/330px-StGenevieve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genevieve","wikidata":"Q235863"},{"title":"Genevieve (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Genevieve is a 1953 British comedy film produced and directed by Henry Cornelius and written by William Rose. It stars John Gregson, Dinah Sheridan, Kenneth More and Kay Kendall as two couples comedically involved in a veteran automobile rally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/33/Genevieve_original_1953_film_poster.jpg/330px-Genevieve_original_1953_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genevieve_(film)","wikidata":"Q826565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Painting_of_Ste_Genevieve_in_the_Church_of_Ste_Genevieve_in_Ste_Genevieve_MO.jpg/500px-Painting_of_Ste_Genevieve_in_the_Church_of_Ste_Genevieve_in_Ste_Genevieve_MO.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Painting_of_Ste_Genevieve_in_the_Church_of_Ste_Genevieve_in_Ste_Genevieve_MO.jpg/1280px-Painting_of_Ste_Genevieve_in_the_Church_of_Ste_Genevieve_in_Ste_Genevieve_MO.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common